  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1135 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nThe cooler and less humid conditions will extend into Thursday,\nwith lows on Thursday morning likely to be in the 60s in parts of\nnortheast Oklahoma and northwest Arkansas. Showers and \nthunderstorms that develop in Kansas Wednesday night in\nassociation with a disturbance moving eastward may graze areas \nnear the Kansas border through the morning and possibly into parts\nof far northwest Arkansas during the afternoon, albeit in a \nlikely declining phase. Temperatures will be warmer on Friday as\nwinds become more southerly, although the actual degree of the\nwarmup should be less than depicted by the NBM due to increasing\ncloud cover and potential for showers. The better rain chances \nfor much of the area will occur Friday night and into Saturday \nwith another disturbance that moves to the southeast along the \nperiphery of the expanding ridge. The amount of shower activity\nand associated cloud cover that lingers into Saturday will impact\nhow hot temperatures get, particularly over parts of far eastern\nOklahoma and western Arkansas. The upper level high remains likely\nto be centered near enough to the region Sunday into early next\nweek to lead to a multi-day period with potential for some triple\ndigit heat and additional heat headlines.",
